WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.152
In the year 1368, Zhu Yuanzhang ascended the throne in Nanjing and proclaimed the founding of the Ming dynasty, opening a new era.

00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:19.646
Civil and military officials offered their congratulations in unison; the people were full of hope, and every street and alley was bustling.

00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:25.996
That same year, the Ming army marched north; its banners blotted out the sun, and its momentum was immense.

00:00:26.346 --> 00:00:31.218
The long column passed through the fields, advancing toward the north.

00:00:31.568 --> 00:00:37.784
The great army arrived below the walls of Dadu, and red flags fluttered before the majestic city gate.

00:00:38.134 --> 00:00:45.886
Emperor Shun of Yuan led his people in retreat to the north, and Yuan rule over the Central Plain thus came to an end.

00:00:46.236 --> 00:00:54.324
The morning sun rose, and golden light lit up the new capital; Chinese history turned to a new chapter, the Ming.

00:00:54.674 --> 00:00:59.834
White cranes soared across the blue sky, symbolising new hope.

